 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Parts of LSTM - Detailed Explanation\n",
    "\n",
    "LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) consists of several key components that work together to solve the problems of basic RNNs. Let's explore each part in detail."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Table of Contents\n",
    "\n",
    "1. [Overview of LSTM Components](#1-overview-of-lstm-components)\n",
    "2. [Cell State (Memory)](#2-cell-state-memory)\n",
    "3. [Hidden State](#3-hidden-state)\n",
    "4. [Forget Gate](#4-forget-gate)\n",
    "5. [Input Gate](#5-input-gate)\n",
    "6. [Candidate Values](#6-candidate-values)\n",
    "7. [Cell State Update](#7-cell-state-update)\n",
    "8. [Output Gate](#8-output-gate)\n",
    "9. [Complete LSTM Cell](#9-complete-lstm-cell)\n",
    "10. [How Parts Work Together](#10-how-parts-work-together)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Overview of LSTM Components\n",
    "\n",
    "LSTM has 4 main parts:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│                                                         │\n",
    "│   1. Cell State (C_t)     - Long-term memory storage   │\n",
    "│                                                         │\n",
    "│   2. Hidden State (h_t)   - Short-term output state    │\n",
    "│                                                         │\n",
    "│   3. Three Gates:                                       │\n",
    "│      • Forget Gate (f_t)   - What to forget            │\n",
    "│      • Input Gate (i_t)    - What to remember           │\n",
    "│      • Output Gate (o_t)   - What to output             │\n",
    "│                                                         │\n",
    "│   4. Candidate Values (C̃_t) - New memory candidates    │\n",
    "│                                                         │\n",
    "└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Visual Overview:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "                    │                                      │\n",
    "  h_{t-1} ─────────┤                                      │\n",
    "                    │      ┌──────────────────────────┐   │\n",
    "  x_t  ────────────┤      │   ┌─────────────────┐    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │                 │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │  FORGET GATE    │────┼───┼───► C_{t-1} × f_t\n",
    "                    │      │   │  f_t = σ(...)   │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   └─────────────────┘    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │           │             │   │\n",
    "                    │      │           ▼             │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   ┌─────────────────┐    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │                 │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │  INPUT GATE     │────┼───┼───► i_t × C̃_t\n",
    "                    │      │   │  i_t = σ(...)   │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   └─────────────────┘    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │           │             │   │\n",
    "                    │      │           ▼             │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   ┌─────────────────┐    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │                 │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │  CANDIDATE      │────┼───┼───► C̃_t\n",
    "                    │      │   │  C̃_t = tanh(...) │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   └─────────────────┘    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │           │             │   │\n",
    "                    │      │           ▼             │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   ┌─────────────────┐    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │  CELL STATE     │────┼───┼───► C_t\n",
    "                    │      │   │  C_t = f_t*C +   │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │       i_t*C̃_t   │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   └─────────────────┘    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │           │             │   │\n",
    "                    │      │           ▼             │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   ┌─────────────────┐    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │                 │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   │  OUTPUT GATE    │────┼───┼───► h_t\n",
    "                    │      │   │  o_t = σ(...)   │    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │   └─────────────────┘    │   │\n",
    "                    │      │                          │   │\n",
    "                    │      └──────────────────────────┘   │\n",
    "                    │                                      │\n",
    "                    └──────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Cell State (Memory)\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is Cell State?\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Cell State (C_t)** is the most important component of LSTM. It acts as the **long-term memory** of the network.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "C_t: [c_1, c_2, c_3, ..., c_h]\n",
    "     \n",
    "     where h = hidden size\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Key Characteristics:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Property | Description |\n",
    "|----------|-------------|\n",
    "| **Shape** | Vector of same size as hidden state |\n",
    "| **Purpose** | Store long-term information |\n",
    "| **Flow** | Runs straight through the chain (conveyor belt) |\n",
    "| **Modification** | Modified by forget and input gates |\n",
    "| **Gradient** | Gradients flow unchanged (solves vanishing gradient) |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Why Cell State is Important?\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "RNN vs LSTM Memory:\n",
    "\n",
    "RNN:\n",
    "  h_1 → h_2 → h_3 → h_4 → h_5 → h_6\n",
    "        ↑\n",
    "        Info from h_2 is transformed at each step\n",
    "        Eventually becomes unrecognizable\n",
    "\n",
    "LSTM:\n",
    "  C_1 ──────────────────────────► C_6  (Conveyor belt)\n",
    "        ↑                         ↑\n",
    "  h_1  │                    h_6   │\n",
    "        ▼                         ▼\n",
    "  Gates add/remove info without  \n",
    "  transforming the entire stream\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Cell State Role:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Carrier of Information** - Holds all relevant past information\n",
    "2. **Gradient Highway** - Allows gradients to flow unchanged\n",
    "3. **Selective Memory** - Only keeps what gates decide is important\n",
    "4. **Prevents Overwriting** - Unlike RNN, doesn't replace, only updates"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Mathematical Representation:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "C_t ∈ R^h\n",
    "\n",
    "Update Formula:\n",
    "C_t = f_t ⊙ C_{t-1} + i_t ⊙ C̃_t\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "  f_t = forget gate (what to keep)\n",
    "  i_t = input gate (what to add)\n",
    "  C̃_t = candidate values (new info)\n",
    "  ⊙ = element-wise multiplication\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Hidden State\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is Hidden State?\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Hidden State (h_t)** is the **short-term/output state** of the LSTM. It contains the information that will be passed to the next time step and used for predictions.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "h_t: [h_1, h_2, h_3, ..., h_h]\n",
    "     \n",
    "     where h = hidden size\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Key Characteristics:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Property | Description |\n",
    "|----------|-------------|\n",
    "| **Shape** | Same size as cell state |\n",
    "| **Purpose** | Short-term memory, output to next layer |\n",
    "| **Flow** | Passed to next time step |\n",
    "| **Generation** | Based on cell state and output gate |\n",
    "| **Usage** | Used for predictions or as input to next layer |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Difference: Cell State vs Hidden State\n",
    "\n",
    "| Aspect | Cell State (C_t) | Hidden State (h_t) |\n",
    "|--------|------------------|-------------------|\n",
    "| **Role** | Long-term memory | Short-term/output |\n",
    "| **Visibility** | Internal | External (output) |\n",
    "| **Gradient** | Unchanged flow | Transformed |\n",
    "| **Gates** | Not directly visible | Controls gates |\n",
    "| **Content** | Raw memory values | Filtered memory |\n",
    "| **Purpose** | Store information | Provide output |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Hidden State Generation:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "h_t = o_t ⊙ tanh(C_t)\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "  o_t = output gate (controls what to output)\n",
    "  C_t = cell state (memory)\n",
    "  tanh = activation function (squashes values to [-1, 1])\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Explanation:**\n",
    "1. `tanh(C_t)` - Squashes cell state values to [-1, 1]\n",
    "2. `o_t ⊙ tanh(C_t)` - Multiply by output gate\n",
    "3. Result is the **filtered, relevant** information for this time step"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. Forget Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is Forget Gate?\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Forget Gate (f_t)** is a neural network layer that decides **what information to discard** from the cell state. It is the first gate to process the input.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "f_t = σ(W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_f)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Architecture:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "       h_{t-1}\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "     ┌─────────┐\n",
    "     │ Concat  │◄──── x_t\n",
    "     │         │\n",
    "     └─────────┘\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "     ┌─────────┐\n",
    "     │   σ    │\n",
    "     │(Sigmoid)│\n",
    "     └─────────┘\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "         f_t\n",
    "    (values 0 to 1)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### How Forget Gate Works:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Step 1: Concatenate previous hidden state and current input\n",
    "        [h_{t-1}, x_t] → shape: (d_h + d_x)\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 2: Multiply by weight matrix and add bias\n",
    "        W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_f → shape: (d_h)\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 3: Apply sigmoid activation\n",
    "        σ(result) → values between 0 and 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 4: Multiply with previous cell state\n",
    "        f_t ⊙ C_{t-1} → what to keep from past\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "f_t = [0.9, 0.1, 0.5, 0.8, 0.2]\n",
    "C_{t-1} = [0.5, 0.8, 0.3, 0.7, 0.9]\n",
    "\n",
    "Result:\n",
    "  Position 1: 0.9 × 0.5 = 0.45  (Keep 90%)\n",
    "  Position 2: 0.1 × 0.8 = 0.08  (Forget 90%)\n",
    "  Position 3: 0.5 × 0.3 = 0.15  (Keep 50%)\n",
    "  Position 4: 0.8 × 0.7 = 0.56  (Keep 80%)\n",
    "  Position 5: 0.2 × 0.9 = 0.18  (Forget 80%)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Real-World Analogy:\n",
    "\n",
    "Think of Forget Gate as a **trash collector**:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Cell State Memory: \"I lived in Paris from 2010-2015, then moved to London, then Berlin.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Forgetting Logic: \"Now I'm planning a trip to Japan, so I don't need European city details.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "After Forget Gate: \"I lived in Europe. (some vague info) Planning trip to Japan.\"\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 5. Input Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is Input Gate?\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Input Gate (i_t)** decides **what new information to store** in the cell state. It works together with the candidate values.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "i_t = σ(W_i · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_i)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Architecture:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "       h_{t-1}\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "     ┌─────────┐\n",
    "     │ Concat  │◄──── x_t\n",
    "     │         │\n",
    "     └─────────┘\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "     ┌─────────┐\n",
    "     │   σ    │\n",
    "     │(Sigmoid)│\n",
    "     └─────────┘\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "         i_t\n",
    "    (values 0 to 1)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### How Input Gate Works:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Step 1: Concatenate previous hidden state and current input\n",
    "        [h_{t-1}, x_t] → shape: (d_h + d_x)\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 2: Multiply by weight matrix and add bias\n",
    "        W_i · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_i → shape: (d_h)\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 3: Apply sigmoid activation\n",
    "        σ(result) → values between 0 and 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 4: Decide which values to update\n",
    "        i_t = 1 means \"update here\"\n",
    "        i_t = 0 means \"don't update\"\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Input Gate vs Forget Gate:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Aspect | Forget Gate | Input Gate |\n",
    "|--------|-------------|------------|\n",
    "| **Purpose** | What to remove | What to add |\n",
    "| **Operation** | Multiply with C_{t-1} | Multiply with C̃_t |\n",
    "| **Values** | 0 = forget all | 0 = add nothing |\n",
    "| **Formula** | f_t ⊙ C_{t-1} | i_t ⊙ C̃_t |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Real-World Analogy:\n",
    "\n",
    "Think of Input Gate as a **teacher marking a notebook**:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "Teacher (Input Gate): \"This information is important, write it down.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "i_t = [1, 0, 1, 1, 0]\n",
    "\n",
    "Position 1: ✓ Write new info\n",
    "Position 2: ✗ Skip (already have this)\n",
    "Position 3: ✓ Write new info\n",
    "Position 4: ✓ Write new info\n",
    "Position 5: ✗ Skip (irrelevant)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 6. Candidate Values\n",
    "\n",
    "### What are Candidate Values?\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Candidate Values (C̃_t)** are the **new information** that could potentially be added to the cell state. They are generated from the current input and previous hidden state.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "C̃_t = tanh(W_c · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_c)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Architecture:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "       h_{t-1}\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "     ┌─────────┐\n",
    "     │ Concat  │◄──── x_t\n",
    "     │         │\n",
    "     └─────────┘\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "     ┌─────────┐\n",
    "     │  tanh   │\n",
    "     │(Hyperbolic│\n",
    "     │ tangent) │\n",
    "     └─────────┘\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "        C̃_t\n",
    "   (values -1 to +1)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Why tanh Instead of sigmoid?\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Sigmoid:  Output range [0, 1]\n",
    "          Used for gates (keep/forget importance)\n",
    "\n",
    "Tanh:     Output range [-1, +1]\n",
    "          Used for candidate values (actual content)\n",
    "          - Allows negative values (inhibitory)\n",
    "          - Zero-centered (better gradient flow)\n",
    "          - Can express full range of information\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Candidate Values in Context:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "C̃_t = tanh(W_c · [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
    "\n",
    "Think of it as: \"Based on current context, here's what might be worth remembering\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "  Current word: \"Paris\"\n",
    "  Context: \"Travel\", \"France\"\n",
    "  Candidate: \"City in France\" (positive)\n",
    "\n",
    "  Current word: \"Spider\"\n",
    "  Context: \"Fear\", \"Scream\"\n",
    "  Candidate: \"Scary creature\" (negative)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 7. Cell State Update\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is Cell State Update?\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Cell State Update** is the process of **modifying the cell state** by combining the forgotten past information with the new candidate information.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "C_t = (f_t ⊙ C_{t-1}) + (i_t ⊙ C̃_t)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step-by-Step Process:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "Step 1: FORGET\n",
    "         f_t ⊙ C_{t-1}\n",
    "         \n",
    "         \"What old information to discard?\"\n",
    "         \n",
    "Step 2: ADD\n",
    "         i_t ⊙ C̃_t\n",
    "         \n",
    "         \"What new information to add?\"\n",
    "         \n",
    "Step 3: COMBINE\n",
    "         C_t = (f_t ⊙ C_{t-1}) + (i_t ⊙ C̃_t)\n",
    "         \n",
    "         \"Merge past memory with new facts\"\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Detailed Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Let's say we're reading a story:\n",
    "\n",
    "Previous Memory (C_{t-1}):\n",
    "  \"John lived in [Paris: 0.9] [London: 0.7] [NewYork: 0.3]\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Forget Gate (f_t):\n",
    "  \"John is now retired, so city details don't matter\"\n",
    "  f_t = [0.1, 0.1, 0.1]\n",
    "\n",
    "After Forgetting:\n",
    "  C_forgotten = f_t ⊙ C_{t-1}\n",
    "  = [0.1×0.9, 0.1×0.7, 0.1×0.3]\n",
    "  = [0.09, 0.07, 0.03]\n",
    "\n",
    "New Information (C̃_t):\n",
    "  \"John retired in 2020, enjoys golf\"\n",
    "  C̃_t = [0.2, 0.8, 0.5] (golf, retired, 2020)\n",
    "\n",
    "Input Gate (i_t):\n",
    "  \"Retirement info is important, daily details less so\"\n",
    "  i_t = [0.9, 0.1, 0.6]\n",
    "\n",
    "New Memory (C_t):\n",
    "  C_t = [0.09, 0.07, 0.03] + [0.9×0.2, 0.1×0.8, 0.6×0.5]\n",
    "  C_t = [0.09, 0.07, 0.03] + [0.18, 0.08, 0.30]\n",
    "  C_t = [0.27, 0.15, 0.33]\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Why Addition is Key?\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "This is the MOST IMPORTANT mathematical insight of LSTM:\n",
    "\n",
    "C_t = C_{t-1} + new_information\n",
    "        ↑\n",
    "        This addition (not replacement!) is why:\n",
    "        1. Gradients flow unchanged\n",
    "        2. Information accumulates\n",
    "        3. No vanishing gradient\n",
    "\n",
    "Derivative of addition is ALWAYS 1:\n",
    "  ∂C_t/∂C_{t-1} = 1\n",
    "        \n",
    "This means gradient doesn't shrink during backpropagation!\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 8. Output Gate\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is Output Gate?\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Output Gate (o_t)** decides **what part of the cell state to output** as the hidden state. It controls what information is relevant for the current time step.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "o_t = σ(W_o · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_o)\n",
    "h_t = o_t ⊙ tanh(C_t)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Architecture:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "       h_{t-1}\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "     ┌─────────┐\n",
    "     │ Concat  │◄──── x_t\n",
    "     │         │\n",
    "     └─────────┘\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "     ┌─────────┐\n",
    "     │   σ    │\n",
    "     │(Sigmoid)│\n",
    "     └─────────┘\n",
    "          │\n",
    "          ▼\n",
    "         o_t\n",
    "    (values 0 to 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "Then:\n",
    "        o_t ⊙ tanh(C_t) = h_t\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### How Output Gate Works:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Step 1: Compute output gate values\n",
    "        o_t = σ(W_o · [h_{t-1}, x_t])\n",
    "        o_t ∈ [0, 1]^h\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 2: Process cell state through tanh\n",
    "        tanh(C_t) ∈ [-1, +1]^h\n",
    "        Why tanh? Squashes values, makes output focused\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 3: Multiply (filter)\n",
    "        h_t = o_t ⊙ tanh(C_t)\n",
    "        o_t = 1 → show this memory\n",
    "        o_t = 0 → hide this memory\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Why tanh Before Output?\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "h_t = o_t ⊙ tanh(C_t)\n",
    "              ↑\n",
    "       Why tanh, not just C_t?\n",
    "\n",
    "Reason 1: \"Focus the mind\"\n",
    "  - C_t may have values ranging widely\n",
    "  - tanh squashes to [-1, 1]\n",
    "  - Makes hidden state more normalized\n",
    "\n",
    "Reason 2: \"Express sentiment clearly\"\n",
    "  - tanh(-1) = negative feeling\n",
    "  - tanh(0) = neutral\n",
    "  - tanh(+1) = positive feeling\n",
    "\n",
    "Reason 3: \"Better gradient flow\"\n",
    "  - tanh has stronger gradients than identity\n",
    "  - Helps in learning\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Real-World Analogy:\n",
    "\n",
    "Think of Output Gate as a **speaker choosing words**:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "Cell State Memory: \"I know French, Spanish, Python, Java, Paris, London, soccer, tennis...\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Context (h_{t-1}, x_t): \"Talking about programming\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Output Gate Decision: \"Focus on programming languages, ignore the rest\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Output (h_t): \"I know Python and Java\"\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 9. Complete LSTM Cell\n",
    "\n",
    "### All Components Together:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Input:     h_{t-1} (previous hidden state)\n",
    "           x_t (current input)\n",
    "\n",
    "Output:    h_t (new hidden state)\n",
    "           C_t (new cell state)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Complete Equations:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│                                                             │\n",
    "│  1. Forget Gate:                                           │\n",
    "│     f_t = σ(W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_f)                    │\n",
    "│                                                             │\n",
    "│  2. Input Gate:                                             │\n",
    "│     i_t = σ(W_i · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_i)                    │\n",
    "│                                                             │\n",
    "│  3. Candidate Values:                                       │\n",
    "│     C̃_t = tanh(W_c · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_c)                 │\n",
    "│                                                             │\n",
    "│  4. Cell State Update:                                      │\n",
    "│     C_t = f_t ⊙ C_{t-1} + i_t ⊙ C̃_t                        │\n",
    "│                                                             │\n",
    "│  5. Output Gate:                                            │\n",
    "│     o_t = σ(W_o · [h_{t-1}, x_t] + b_o)                    │\n",
    "│                                                             │\n",
    "│  6. Hidden State:                                           │\n",
    "│     h_t = o_t ⊙ tanh(C_t)                                  │\n",
    "│                                                             │\n",
    "└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Parameter Count:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "Each gate has:\n",
    "  - Weight matrix: (d_h, d_h + d_x)\n",
    "  - Bias vector: (d_h,)\n",
    "\n",
    "Total for 4 operations (f, i, C̃, o):\n",
    "  - Weight matrices: 4 × d_h × (d_h + d_x)\n",
    "  - Bias vectors: 4 × d_h\n",
    "\n",
    "Total Parameters = 4 × d_h × (d_h + d_x) + 4 × d_h\n",
    "                  = 4 × d_h × (d_h + d_x + 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "  If d_h = 256 and d_x = 512\n",
    "  Total = 4 × 256 × (256 + 512 + 1)\n",
    "        = 4 × 256 × 769\n",
    "        = 787,456 parameters\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Visual Summary:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "                    INPUTS\n",
    "                    h_{t-1}\n",
    "                      x_t\n",
    "                       │\n",
    "                       ▼\n",
    "              ┌──────────────────┐\n",
    "              │                  │\n",
    "              │  ┌────────────┐  │\n",
    "              │  │  FORGET    │  │\n",
    "              │  │    f_t     │  │\n",
    "              │  └────────────┘  │\n",
    "              │         │        │\n",
    "              │  ┌────────────┐  │\n",
    "              │  │  INPUT     │  │\n",
    "              │  │    i_t     │  │\n",
    "              │  └────────────┘  │\n",
    "              │         │        │\n",
    "              │  ┌────────────┐  │\n",
    "              │  │ CANDIDATE  │  │\n",
    "              │  │    C̃_t     │  │\n",
    "              │  └────────────┘  │\n",
    "              │         │        │\n",
    "              │         ▼        │\n",
    "              │  ┌────────────┐  │\n",
    "              │  │  CELL      │  │\n",
    "              │  │  STATE     │  │\n",
    "              │  │   C_t      │  │\n",
    "              │  └────────────┘  │\n",
    "              │         │        │\n",
    "              │  ┌────────────┐  │\n",
    "              │  │  OUTPUT    │  │\n",
    "              │  │    o_t     │  │\n",
    "              │  └────────────┘  │\n",
    "              │         │        │\n",
    "              └─────────│────────┘\n",
    "                        │\n",
    "                        ▼\n",
    "                      h_t\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 10. How Parts Work Together\n",
    "\n",
    "### Complete Example: Sentence Processing\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "Sentence: \"John lived in Paris. He spoke French.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Goal: When we see \"He\", we know it refers to \"John\"\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Time Step 1: \"John\"\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Input: x_1 = \"John\"\n",
    "Previous: h_0 = [0, 0, 0, ...], C_0 = [0, 0, 0, ...]\n",
    "\n",
    "Forget Gate: f_1 = [0, 0, 0, ...] (nothing to forget)\n",
    "\n",
    "Candidate: C̃_1 = [0.9, 0.1, 0.2, ...] (John is a person)\n",
    "\n",
    "Input Gate: i_1 = [1, 1, 1, ...] (definitely store this)\n",
    "\n",
    "Cell State: C_1 = [0.9, 0.1, 0.2, ...] (stored: \"person name\")\n",
    "\n",
    "Output Gate: o_1 = [0.8, 0.2, 0.3, ...] (show person info)\n",
    "\n",
    "Hidden State: h_1 = [0.7, 0.1, 0.2, ...] (output: person info)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Time Step 2: \"lived\"\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Input: x_2 = \"lived\"\n",
    "Previous: h_1 = [...], C_1 = [0.9, 0.1, 0.2, ...]\n",
    "\n",
    "Forget Gate: f_2 = [0.9, 0.8, 0.9, ...] (keep person info)\n",
    "\n",
    "Candidate: C̃_2 = [0.1, 0.5, 0.2, ...] (verb info)\n",
    "\n",
    "Input Gate: i_2 = [0.5, 0.3, 0.5, ...] (store some)\n",
    "\n",
    "Cell State: C_2 = [0.9×0.9, 0.1×0.8, 0.2×0.9] + [0.1×0.5, 0.5×0.3, 0.2×0.5]\n",
    "          = [0.81+0.05, 0.08+0.15, 0.18+0.10]\n",
    "          = [0.86, 0.23, 0.28] (kept: person, added: verb)\n",
    "\n",
    "Hidden State: h_2 = [0.6, 0.1, 0.2, ...] (output)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Time Step 3-5: \"in\", \"Paris\", \".\"\n",
    "\n",
    "```\",
    "Cell state accumulates location info\n",
    "After processing: C_5 = [0.85, 0.22, 0.75, ...]\n",
    "                               ↑      ↑\n",
    "                           person   location\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Time Step 6: \"He\"\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Input: x_6 = \"He\"\n",
    "Previous: h_5 = [...], C_5 = [0.85, 0.22, 0.75, ...]\n",
    "\n",
    "Forget Gate: f_6 = [0.95, 0.90, 0.85, ...]\n",
    "             (Keep most info - pronoun needs subject)\n",
    "\n",
    "Candidate: C̃_6 = [0.1, 0.1, 0.1, ...] (pronoun info)\n",
    "\n",
    "Input Gate: i_6 = [0.1, 0.1, 0.1, ...] (minimal new info)\n",
    "\n",
    "Cell State: C_6 ≈ C_5 (mostly preserved!)\n",
    "                           ↑\n",
    "                    CRITICAL: Long-term memory intact\n",
    "\n",
    "Output Gate: o_6 = [0.9, 0.8, 0.6, ...]\n",
    "              (Show subject info since \"He\" needs reference)\n",
    "\n",
    "Hidden State: h_6 contains subject reference (John)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Key Insights:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Why LSTM succeeded where RNN failed:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. FORGET GATE allowed selective deletion\n",
    "   - Removed \"lived in\" details, kept subject\n",
    "\n",
    "2. CELL STATE preserved information\n",
    "   - \"John\" survived through 5 time steps\n",
    "   - Wasn't overwritten at each step\n",
    "\n",
    "3. INPUT GATE controlled new information\n",
    "   - Only important new facts were added\n",
    "\n",
    "4. OUTPUT GATE filtered for relevance\n",
    "   - When processing \"He\", showed subject info\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Summary Table\n",
    "\n",
    "| Component | Symbol | Formula | Purpose |\n",
    "|-----------|--------|---------|---------|\n",
    "| **Cell State** | C_t | C_t = f_t ⊙ C_{t-1} + i_t ⊙ C̃_t | Long-term memory |\n",
    "| **Hidden State** | h_t | h_t = o_t ⊙ tanh(C_t) | Short-term output |\n",
    "| **Forget Gate** | f_t | σ(W_f · [h_{t-1}, x_t]) | What to forget |\n",
    "| **Input Gate** | i_t | σ(W_i · [h_{t-1}, x_t]) | What to add |\n",
    "| **Candidate** | C̃_t | tanh(W_c · [h_{t-1}, x_t]) | New info |\n",
    "| **Output Gate** | o_t | σ(W_o · [h_{t-1}, x_t]) | What to output |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Cell State** is the memory highway - allows long-term information flow\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Forget Gate** decides what old information is irrelevant\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Input Gate** decides what new information is important\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **Candidate Values** generate potential new memories\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **Output Gate** filters the cell state for the current output\n",
    "\n",
    "6. **Hidden State** is the filtered, relevant output for this time step\n",
    "\n",
    "7. **Addition in cell state update** is the key to preventing vanishing gradients"
   ]
  }
